      "id": "7eeddeb79af54141b58e4cffe32d93a5",
      "name": "In Tennessee STAR, small-class assignment raised kindergarten achievement by an estimated 5.36 percentile points.",
      "description": "Compared with regular classes without a full-time aide, the estimated gain in average Stanford test percentile rank was 5.36 points (class-clustered SE 1.21). Krueger (1999), Table V column 7, reports the effect of initial assignment, not a percentage increase in test scores.",
